{
  "slug": "rubber-duck",
  "name": "Rubber Duck",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "rubber-duck is a Socratic thinking partner for Claude Code.\n\nInspired by the classic rubber duck debugging technique—but with a duck that actually talks back—it helps you think through problems instead of just handing you answers.\n\nWhile most AI tools focus on writing code for you, rubber-duck is designed to help you learn it. Rather than giving you the fix, it asks the right question at the right time—guiding you step by step, at your own pace.\n\nUse Claude when you need to ship fast.\nUse rubber-duck when you want to understand what you’re building.\n\nThe best developers use both.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**, **1 agent** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `duck` (Enter Rubber Duck mode — Claude becomes a Socratic thinking partner), `duck-design` (Architecture thinking mode — rubber-duck asks questions about design decisions, constraints, and tradeoffs instead of prescribing a solution), `duck-reveal` (Exit Rubber Duck mode and get the full answer), `duck-sessions` (Show a summary of past Rubber Duck sessions — streaks, peek history, and recent activity), `duck-status` (Show a structured summary of the current rubber-duck session — what you've figured out, what's still open, and…), `rubber-duck` (Socratic thinking partner — invoke when user wants to think through a bug, design decision, or concept themselves…)\n- **Agents** (1): `rubber-duck` (A Socratic thinking partner that helps developers reason through bugs, design decisions, and code understanding by asking questions…)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionEnd`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install rubber-duck@claude-community` from `mo-inkhan/rubber-duck`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 1
  },
